      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The current trend is not merely deciding that climate necessity overrides economic protections but is actively dismantling the very concept of \"fairness\" in urban policy to prioritize collective survival over individual financial hardship. This shift represents a fundamental ideological break where the state prioritizes the survival of the planet and the long-term viability of cities over the immediate economic interests of working-class drivers. Consequently, the old economic objections are no longer treated as valid policy constraints but are instead framed as moral failures of those who refuse to accept the urgent demands of the climate crisis.",
      "source": "target",
